The [[Darksaber]] is a [[Weapon]] normally obtained by combining a [[Lightsaber]] with a [[Corrupted Crystal]]. It deals high base damage and scales off of all debuffs on the opponent. On hit, it spends a {{icon/mana}} to inflict a {{icon/blind}}.

Compared to the [[Lightsaber]], the [[Darksaber]] deals more base damage, has better scaling, and has a better {{icon/blind}}-inflicting ability, although the differences leave room for a [[Lightsaber]] to be better in certain rare situations. The [[Darksaber]] needs {{icon/mana}} to inflict permanent {{icon/blind}}, while the [[Lightsaber]] requires {{icon/regeneration}} to inflict lots of temporary {{icon/blind}}. As such, the [[Lightsaber]] can possibly do more early in the battle, but in a longer fight, the permanent {{icon/blind}} of the [[Darksaber]] would eventually pay off. The [[Darksaber]] also requires the less precious of the two buffs. The debuff scaling of the [[Darksaber]] damage is also far superior compared to the {{icon/blind}} scaling of the [[Lightsaber]], even though the [[Lightsaber]] scales better off of {{icon/blind}} specifically. {{icon/blind}} is just too rare and difficult to stack compared to {{icon/cold}} and {{icon/poison}}, so the practical damage-ceiling of the [[Darksaber]] is likely much higher.
